{"actor":"hypothesis","data":{"dependent_variable":"KNN classification accuracy","evidence_ids":["E1"],"expected_direction":"increase","gap_ids":["G1"],"id":"H1","independent_variable":"type of feature distribution (skewed vs. normal)","rationale":"G1 highlights a lack of systematic comparison across feature distributions. E1 shows Z-score standardization outperforms Min–Max in accuracy on the date fruit dataset, which may have skewed features. This hypothesis tests whether standardization's advantage is particularly strong in non-normal data, addressing the narrow scope of current evidence.","statement":"Standardization improves KNN classification accuracy on tabular datasets with skewed or non-normally distributed features compared to Min–Max normalization."},"hash":"31562f49d95cb403fbb2bb42ebb6d979c4439e262f39106d336f37f48159a0a7","kind":"artefact","prev":"6a96717200083c1b160f729b0e4552c13c8612b0634c00ca4f5f8405b8232dba","seq":30,"stage":"hypotheses","ts":"2026-10-10T03:22:59.016+00:00"}
{"actor":"hypothesis","data":{"dependent_variable":"KNN classification accuracy","evidence_ids":["E2","E5"],"expected_direction":"increase","gap_ids":["G2"],"id":"H2","independent_variable":"distance metric (Euclidean, Manhattan)","rationale":"G2 points to insufficient investigation of interactions between standardization and hyperparameters like distance metric. E2 shows optimized KNN with feature scaling achieves high accuracy, and E5 introduces scaling in distance computation—suggesting interaction with distance metric. This hypothesis tests if standardization’s benefit is amplified with specific metrics.","statement":"The accuracy improvement from standardization in KNN is dependent on the choice of distance metric (e.g., Euclidean vs. Manhattan), with Euclidean benefiting most from standardization."},"hash":"78e55130ac8e18d81f9962cabe89919a1e9fdc7f1b0eb9bde308229ffd417d16","kind":"artefact","prev":"31562f49d95cb403fbb2bb42ebb6d979c4439e262f39106d336f37f48159a0a7","seq":31,"stage":"hypotheses","ts":"2026-10-10T03:22:59.016+00:00"}
